    "result_text": "Done. Both the new acceptance test and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## What I did\n\nThe task was to return `capacityWarning: true` on owner responses when the owner's city already holds 40\u201349 owners (approaching the hard limit of 50, which is unchanged).\n\n**Two files touched, no existing function modified** \u2014 keeping structural impact minimal:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `capacityWarning` boolean to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gets a `setCapacityWarning`/`getCapacityWarning` (data-only edit, no function changed).\n\n2. **New `OwnerCapacityWarningAdvice.java`** \u2014 a small, self-contained `@Aspect` modeled exactly on the existing `OwnerBulkSignupWarningAdvice`. It runs `@AfterReturning` on `addOwner`/`getOwner`, counts owners in the same city (case-insensitively, whitespace collapsed \u2014 matching the existing hard-limit advice's `normalize`), and sets `capacityWarning` true only when the count is in `[40, 49]`.\n\nThis adds the behaviour as a fresh cohesive unit with zero surrounding class complexity (`WMC_other = 0`) rather than growing the existing hard-rejection `OwnerCityCapacityAdvice` or the controller/mapper. The hard rejection at 50 is left untouched.",
